    "## 3. Analysis Plan\n",
    "\n",
    "| Stage | Steps | Output |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| 1. EDA | Missing values, duplicates, class distributions, narrative length | Clean dataset, EDA figures |\n",
    "| 2. Preprocessing | Lowercase, remove noise, stopwords, lemmatise | Clean corpus |\n",
    "| 3. Sentiment labelling | Keyword scoring + company response signals | Labelled dataset |\n",
    "| 4. Topic modelling | CountVectorizer → LDA (6 topics) | Topic per complaint |\n",
    "| 5. Feature engineering | TF-IDF (5 000 features, unigrams + bigrams) | Feature matrix |\n",
    "| 6. Model training | 75/25 stratified split; LR & NB; 5-fold CV | Trained models |\n",
    "| 7. Evaluation | Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, Confusion Matrix | Metrics & model selection |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why weighted F1 is the primary metric:** Sentiment classes are imbalanced (most complaints are negative). Accuracy alone would be misleading — a model that always predicts \"Negative\" would score high but be useless. Weighted F1 balances precision and recall across all classes (Tan, Steinbach and Kumar, 2019)."
   ]
