    "## 7. Feature Engineering — TF-IDF for Sentiment Classification\n",
    "\n",
    "For the **supervised** sentiment classification task we use TF-IDF instead of raw counts. TF-IDF down-weights words that appear in every document and up-weights distinctive words this generally gives better classification features (Manning, Raghavan and Schütze, 2008).\n",
    "\n",
    "Key choices:\n",
    "- `max_features=5000` — keeps the 5 000 most informative terms\n",
    "- `ngram_range=(1,2)` — captures bigrams like \"does not\" so negation isn't lost\n",
    "- `sublinear_tf=True` — log-scales term frequency to reduce the influence of very frequent terms\n",
    "- `class_weight=\"balanced\"` on the LR model — corrects for the class imbalance we saw in Section 6"
   ]
