   "source": [
    "**Interpretation:**\n",
    "- **Weighted F1** is the primary metric because classes are imbalanced\n",
    "- Both models perform strongly on the majority **Negative** class but weaker on the minority **Positive** class — this is expected given the skew in training data, not a model failure\n",
    "- The confusion matrix shows Neutral and Positive complaints are more likely to be confused with each other than either is with Negative — Negative language is much more distinctive\n",
    "- **5-fold CV** confirms the result is stable and not just lucky on one train/test split\n",
    "- For the client, **Recall on Negative matters most**: missing real dissatisfaction is more costly than flagging a borderline case"
   ]
